    "difficultyReason": "No graph or direct rate is supplied for US dollars to euros. The student must see that the conversion goes through Australian dollars: divide 260 by 0.65 to get A$400, then multiply by 0.6. This is two linked steps with a direction decision (divide, then multiply) and some decimal arithmetic. That is more than the signposted single-rate work in p9-q6. It is less than the open-ended listing and optimising in A4.",
